    "_metadata": {
     "name": "Patrick Kane",
     "description": "Patrick Kane's return to Chicago was a poignant and emotional event for both him and Blackhawks fans. For the first time, he was on the ice as a member of the opposing team. During a stoppage in the first period, the Chicago crowd gave him a lengthy standing ovation, honoring his 16 seasons with the team and his role in winning three Stanley Cups. Later in a dramatic finish, Kane scored the game-winning goal in overtime on a breakaway. After celebration of the goal, Kane stayed on the ice, raising his stick and clapping to show his appreciation for the fans.\r\n\r\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
